<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nur ibn Mujahid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1550–1567</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nur ibn Mujahid was a ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> from 1550 to 1567, following the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Imam Ahmad</a> ibn Ibrahim. He governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harar">Harar</a> and built its defensive wall, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugol">Jugol</a>. He could not restore the institutional coherence of Ahmad's state, and Adal was reduced to a regional power conducting annual raids.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nur-ibn-mujahid.jpg" alt="Nur ibn Mujahid" width="277" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A. Davey from Where I Live Now: Pacific Northwest · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Streets_of_Harar,_Ethiopia_(2203217018).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
